:8","global_turn_index":359,"locator":"[S21T8]","raw_turn_sha256":"c7f83b2bf999e061bf84e8f08e1982c89e7521737b235e00f44dc11a3505e72e","rendered_turn_sha256":"2ae35b839e17c717a026560ef879d00087e9598a32cc6d15848b242ba1773669","session_date":"2023-10-04","session_datetime":"2023-10-04T14:44:00","session_id":"session_21","session_index":21,"source_sha256":"e263a8896b9113380280c3157a7b76afd37a76c5ed6b6aa2b8a8a3edb7e622cc","speaker":"Dave","turn_index":8},{"dia_id":"D26:2","global_turn_index":457,"locator":"[S26T2]","raw_turn_sha256":"0ba18d92b5f1fa0f365e0eefd2a45b277b57e34b09ee06e6120a7af0dc3048ee","rendered_turn_sha256":"b1744a00170fef82c808ba2da8607d9fcd2774ed644622f1ae5a4fd03d92da0a","session_date":"2023-10-25","session_datetime":"2023-10-25T20:25:00","session_id":"session_26","session_index":26,"source_sha256":"06d99733973749a159c60e335c05129567ae4d555ec087231b21af1ed317b66c","speaker":"Dave","turn_index":2},{"dia_id":"D26:3","global_turn_index":458,"locator":"[S26T3]","raw_turn_sha256":"fe45878bd84eaf33303fc8df61a3466b8d3f9aba50e7e0059e9bb35af97b2c5d","rendered_turn_sha256":"ce74130c6f859ab8100a8fda2bab30a2169c0aac5e80d5ebf110f8b4d668728b","session_date":"2023-10-25","session_datetime":"2023-10-25T20:25:00","session_id":"session_26","session_index":26,"source_sha256":"0c7ea61ab88bf9a8d4f8a51e1d1b783e2914d46e97d9bc1a4f66c5718902e3e1","speaker":"Calvin","turn_index":3}],"speaker":null,"store_id":"s3","store_snapshot_sha256":"983238fddc77a88ef4ae3d06b50bcfd25a429f497e89c6af4d9477cefca9cad2","text":"- On 2023-08-11, got picked for a car mod workshop — called it \"a dream come true\", since he's always wanted to learn auto engineering and work on building a custom car (ties to his stated dream of building a custom car from scratch, see ## Classic cars); Calvin congratulated him [S13T1][S13T3].\n- Shared a photo of himself standing in front of a car on a lift at the workshop [S13T1].\n- Shared a photo of the \"really thrilling part of the workshop\" — a mechanic working on a car — saying \"seeing the potential come to life is always satisfying\" [S13T5].\n- Current car project: has been doing engine swaps and suspension modifications, and is now learning body modifications; the project is giving a classic muscle car a modern twist — \"a challenge but so fun\" — and shared a photo of a silver Corvette parked in front of a building; Calvin praised the modern twist the silver finish gives [S13T7][S13T8].\n- Later in the same 2023-08-11 conversation, Dave explained the project's goal: he wanted \"a modern vibe but also that classic muscle car style\", and is \"really happy with it\"; \"It's all about those small details that make it unique and personalized\", and the project is about showing his style — \"it's like customizing a work of art on wheels\"; Calvin praised the work and attention to detail (\"You've really put in some work! That attention to detail is great\"), agreed the small details are what make a masterpiece unique and personalized, and told Dave to \"keep coming up with new cool stuff, bud\", saying he's excited to see what Dave will do next [S13T9][S13T10][S13T11][S13T12][S13T13][S13T14].\n- On 2023-08-14, told Calvin the project is \"going great\" and shared a photo of the car he's restoring (a car with a broken engine in the woods) — \"It's pretty cool seeing it go from a beat-up mess to a real beauty.\" Calvin asked how long it would take to restore; Dave hopes it'll be all fixed up by the end of next month (end of September 2023): \"Lots of elbow grease but it'll be worth the transformation.\" [S14T11][S14T12][S14T13]\n- On 2023-09-15, told Calvin it's \"been awesome\": \"Been restoring this vintage beauty\" and shared the \"final result\" photo — a man standing next to a classic car — implying the restoration he had been updating Calvin on since 2023-08-14 (above) is now finished, ahead of his earlier hope (stated 2023-08-14) to have it done by the end of September 2023; Calvin: \"Nice work, Dave! That looks amazing. Is it satisfying to see your hard work pay off?\" [S19T7][S19T8]; Dave: \"It's so satisfying to see this brought back to life,\" especially seeing people's reactions when they see the finished product — \"makes all the hard work worth it\" [S19T9].\n- On 2023-09-22, reported a setback on the vintage Mustang (the restoration car he had been updating Calvin on — see above; he had shown the \"final result\" on 2023-09-15): he had been working on the engine and thought he'd fixed it, but when he started the car up he heard a weird noise — \"So disappointing after putting so much work in\"; shared a photo of the engine (a car engine with a small engine) and asked Calvin \"Take a look at the engine!\" [S20T1].\n- On 2023-10-04, told Calvin he's been working on the Ford Mustang he found in a junkyard (the restoration car he has been updating Calvin on, see above) — \"it was in bad shape, but I knew it had potential\"; he said working on cars really helps him relax — \"it's therapeutic to see them come back to life\" — answering Calvin's question about what hobbies help him relax [S21T4].\n- On 2023-10-04, after Calvin asked for pictures of the restoration looking amazing (\"I'd love to see how it turned out!\"), shared a photo of a red car parked in a field with other cars — \"I put in a lot of work restoring it, but the result is awesome. It's so satisfying to bring an old car back to life.\" [S21T5][S21T6].\n- On 2023-10-04, shared a photo of his own hands after a day in the garage — \"permanently stained with grease. But it's worth it when you see the end result.\" [S21T8].\n- On 2023-10-25, told Calvin he recently attended a conference in Detroit — \"it was so cool, I learned a lot\" (Calvin: \"Good to hear that you've learned a lot of new things at the conference in Detroit!\") — his professional learning alongside his San Francisco car workshops, see above (Calvin's side in the 2023-10-25 entry of the Relationships section of this file) [S26T2][S26T3].","text_sha2